description:
Design a D-type flip-flop with enable and reset functionality. The flip-flop captures the input `d` on the rising edge of the clock `clk` when the enable signal `en` is asserted. If the reset signal is high, the output `q` is asynchronously set to LOW. This module effectively functions as a one-bit storage element with control over when to store the input value and the ability to reset the output.
module top_module(
input wire clk, reset,en,
input wire d ,
output reg q
);

