Design a module that performs data alignment and selection for a 64-bit input based on an address and a data mode. The module takes a 3-bit address, a 2-bit data mode, and a 64-bit data input, and produces a 64-bit data output. The lower 32 bits of the output are selected and aligned from the input data based on the provided address and data mode, allowing for byte-level access and control of which data bytes to pass based on the alignment and mode. The upper 32 bits are directly passed through from the input to the output. This functionality is crucial for memory-mapped I/O and data manipulation in digital designs.
