description:
Design a 4-bit binary to Gray code converter that operates on the rising edge of a clock signal. The module takes a 4-bit binary input and generates a 4-bit Gray code output. The Gray code is computed by performing a bitwise XOR operation between the binary input and a right-shifted version of itself. The previous binary value is stored for potential future use, though it is not utilized in the output calculation.
module top_module(
    input [3:0] binary_in,
    input clk,
    output reg [3:0] gray_out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [3:0] binary_in,
    input clk,
    output reg [3:0] gray_out
);reg [3:0] binary_prev;

always @(posedge clk) begin
    binary_prev <= binary_in;
    gray_out <= binary_in ^ (binary_in >> 1);
end

endmodule

